        "# Digital Design - mod-14\n\n",
        "**Course:** digital-design\n\n",
        "Run the code cells below to practice.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Combinational Circuit:\n  Inputs \u2500\u2500\u2192 [Logic] \u2500\u2500\u2192 Outputs\n  (output = f(inputs) only)\n\nSequential Circuit:\n  Inputs \u2500\u2500\u2192 [Logic] \u2500\u2500\u2192 Outputs\n                \u2191    \u2193\n              [Memory/State]\n  (output = f(inputs, current state))\n  (next state = g(inputs, current state))"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Clock waveform:\n      ___     ___     ___     ___\n     |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |\n  ___|   |___|   |___|   |___|   |___\n     \u2191       \u2191       \u2191       \u2191\n   Rising  Rising  Rising  Rising\n   edge    edge    edge    edge\n\nPeriod (T) = time for one complete cycle\nFrequency (f) = 1/T\nDuty cycle = time HIGH / T (typically 50%)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n    \u2502              \u2502\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2192[NOT]\u2500\u2500\u2192Q\u2500\u2500\u2524\n                   \u2502\n    \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2192[NOT]\u2500\u2500\u2192Q'\u2500\u2518\n    \u2502              \n    \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Inputs\n                \u2502\n                \u25bc\n        \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n        \u2502 Combinational \u2502\u2500\u2500\u2192 Outputs\n        \u2502    Logic      \u2502\n        \u2502               \u2502\u2500\u2500\u2192 Next State\n        \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n                \u2191\n           Current State\n                \u2502\n        \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n        \u2502   Memory      \u2502\n        \u2502  (Flip-Flops) \u2502\u2190\u2500\u2500 Clock\n        \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Clock:    ___     ___     ___\n         |   |   |   |   |   |\n      ___|   |___|   |___|   |___\n\nState:  S0  |  S1  |  S2  |  S3\n         (current state changes at each clock edge)\n\nThe sequence: S0 \u2192 S1 \u2192 S2 \u2192 S3 depends on inputs at each clock edge"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "verilog",
          "// Basic sequential element - D flip-flop behavior\nmodule simple_register(\n    input  wire       clk,\n    input  wire       d,\n    output reg        q\n);\n    // State updates ONLY on rising clock edge\n    always @(posedge clk) begin\n        q <= d;    // Non-blocking assignment for sequential logic\n    end\nendmodule"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "verilog",
          "// Sequential vs Combinational in Verilog\nmodule sequential_example(\n    input  wire       clk,\n    input  wire       reset,\n    input  wire       enable,\n    input  wire [3:0] data_in,\n    output reg  [3:0] stored_value,\n    output wire [3:0] doubled\n);\n    // Sequential: updates only on clock edge (has memory)\n    always @(posedge clk) begin\n        if (reset)\n            stored_value <= 4'b0;\n        else if (enable)\n            stored_value <= data_in;\n        // else: stored_value retains its value (MEMORY!)\n    end\n    \n    // Combinational: no clock, no memory\n    assign doubled = stored_value << 1;\nendmodule"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
